Review comment:

- [P2] Require every pinned count entry — /home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/dh2-t1c/scripts/check-governed-surface-pin.sh:197-198
  When a pin omits `counts.allowlist`, `counts.core`, or `counts.recovery_denylist`, `.get()` returns `None` and both this internal-consistency check and the later file-count check silently skip that list. A malformed re-pin can therefore delete a count entry, update the hashes/member list, and still exit 0, defeating the separate count backstop this gate is supposed to enforce.
